tmp

# Stretchly: everything under ~/.config/Stretchly is Electron runtime state
# (caches, cookies, etc.) except the preferences file.
home/config/Stretchly/*
!home/config/Stretchly/config.json

# AnkiWeb credentials, written at runtime by the anki-persist-sync-creds addon
# in home.nix and read back by programs.anki's sync.usernameFile/keyFile.
#
# Only the two secret files are ignored, NOT the directory: xdg.configFile maps
# home/config/* onto ~/.config/* via readDir, and Nix's git+file flake source
# only sees tracked files. Ignore the directory and it becomes invisible to Nix
# ("To make it visible to Nix, run: git add home/config"); force-add it with
# `git add -f` and the key lands in a commit. Instead a placeholder file is
# tracked so the directory exists on a fresh clone, and these two stay out of
# git. See home/config/anki/README.md.
home/config/anki/sync-username
home/config/anki/sync-key

